<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 570–<a href="/years/632">632</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as The Prophet Muhammad, Muhammad ibn Abdullah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad was the prophet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> around 570 and active as a merchant before, according to Islamic tradition, receiving the revelations gathered in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quran">Quran</a> from about 610. Persecution drove him and his followers to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a> in 622, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hijra">hijra</a> from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islamic-calendar">Islamic calendar</a> counts; there he led a growing community as prophet, lawgiver and commander, returning to Mecca in triumph in 630. At his death in 632 most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> acknowledged Islam, and within a century his successors ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p></div>
